Azure Site Recovery supports disaster recovery by helping organizations replicate supported workloads and coordinate recovery when a primary environment becomes unavailable.

Disaster recovery planning considers:

* Recovery Time Objective (RTO)
* Recovery Point Objective (RPO)
* Replication
* Failover
* Failback
* Recovery testing
* Application dependencies

For example, an organization may replicate critical workloads from an on-premises datacenter to Azure so that applications can be recovered if the primary datacenter experiences a major outage.

A real-life use case is a financial institution maintaining a secondary recovery environment to protect critical services from datacenter failures.

Disaster recovery planning improves resilience and reduces the business impact of major infrastructure incidents.
